  "solution": "Given:\n\nA sum amounts to Rs. 6,120 in 2 years and Rs. 7,340 in 3 years\n\nFormula used:\n\nFor CI,\n\nAmount = P [1 + (r/100)]T\n\nCalculation:\n\nFor 2 years, \n\n6120 = P × [1 + (r/100)]²\n\nFor 3 years, \n\n7340 = P × [1 + (r/100)]3\n\n⇒ (P × [1 + (r/100)]³)/(P × [1 + (r/100)]²) = (7340)/(6120)\n\n⇒ 1 + (r/100) = 734/612\n\n⇒ r/100 = (734/612) - 1\n\n⇒ r/100 = 122/612 = 0.1993\n\n⇒ r = 19.93% ≈ 20%\n\nNow, for T = 2, r = 20%, A = 6120\n\n6120 = P × (1 + 20/100)²\n\n⇒ 6120 = P × (6/5)2\n\n⇒ P = 6120 × (25/36)\n\n⇒ P = Rs 4250 approx\n\n**∴ The sum is Rs 4250.**",
